    "result": "## Summary\n\n\u2705 All frai-core tests now pass! Here's what I fixed:\n\n### Issue 1: Missing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` export in governance module\n**File**: `src/finetune/index.js`\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- The test was importing these directly but they weren't exported as named exports, only available on the default export\n\n### Issue 2: Inconsistent metric function signature in eval module\n**File**: `src/eval/metrics.js`\n- Updated `toxicityMetric` signature from `(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms)`\n- The issue: `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` was treating the references array as banned terms, causing all outputs to be flagged as toxic\n- Now the function accepts `references` as a parameter (which it ignores) to be consistent with other metrics like `exactMatchMetric` and `lengthVarianceMetric`\n\n**Test results**: 28 tests passing \u2713 (8 test files, 0 failures)\n**Public API**: All exports remain intact and accessible",
